---
import MarketingLayout from "../layouts/MarketingLayout.astro";
---

<MarketingLayout
  title="Health Disclaimer — Pre"
  description="Health and medical disclaimer for Pre, the sport-specific prehab app."
>
  <main style="background-color: var(--color-bg); min-height: 100svh;">
    <article class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-6 py-16 md:py-24">
      <header class="mb-12">
        <a
          href="/"
          class="mb-8 inline-block text-sm font-medium"
          style="color: var(--color-muted); font-family: var(--font-body);"
        >&larr; Back to Pre</a>
        <h1
          class="mb-4 font-sans text-2xl font-bold leading-tight md:text-3xl"
          style="color: var(--color-text);"
        >Health Disclaimer</h1>
        <p class="text-sm" style="color: var(--color-muted); font-family: var(--font-body);">
          Effective date: May 21, 2026
        </p>
      </header>

      <div class="legal-prose" style="font-family: var(--font-body); color: var(--color-text);">

        <p>
          Pre helps you move better and prepare for training. But there's a hard line we want to be
          completely clear about, because it matters for your safety: Pre is a fitness and prehab tool,
          not a clinician. This page explains what that means before you start using it.
        </p>
        <p>
          Pre is intended only for general fitness, movement preparation, and educational exercise
          guidance. It is not intended to diagnose, treat, cure, or prevent any disease or injury, or to
          make medical decisions.
        </p>

        <h2>Pre is not medical advice</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>Pre is not a medical device, and nothing in it is medical advice.</strong> The
          sessions, exercises, ratings, Coach replies, and recommendations Pre generates are general
          fitness and educational information. They are not a diagnosis, not a treatment plan, and not a
          substitute for the judgment of a qualified healthcare professional who can actually examine
          you.
        </p>

        <h2>Talk to a professional first</h2>
        <p>
          Before you start Pre — or any new exercise program — talk to a physician, physical therapist,
          or other qualified healthcare provider. This is especially important if you:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Have a current or past injury</li>
          <li>Have a medical condition, including heart, joint, bone, or neurological conditions</li>
          <li>Are pregnant, recently gave birth, or recently had surgery</li>
          <li>Are recovering from illness</li>
          <li>Take medication that affects exercise, balance, or heart rate</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          A professional who knows your history can tell you whether the kind of movement Pre suggests is
          right for you. Pre can't do that.
        </p>

        <h2>It can't diagnose or treat an injury</h2>
        <p>
          Pre's body-region capacity ratings are your own self-assessments, not a clinical evaluation.
          Pre uses them to shape general prehab guidance — it does not diagnose injuries, identify their
          cause, or treat them. If you think you're injured, see a healthcare professional. Don't use
          Pre to figure out what's wrong or to decide whether you need care.
        </p>

        <h2>If something hurts, stop</h2>
        <p>
          Listen to your body. If you feel pain, sharp discomfort, dizziness, shortness of breath, or
          anything that doesn't feel right during a session, stop immediately. Don't push through it.
          Rest, and if it continues or concerns you, get it checked out by a professional. Pain is a
          signal, not an obstacle to power through.
        </p>

        <h2>In an emergency</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>Pre is not for emergencies.</strong> If you're having a medical emergency — chest
          pain, trouble breathing, a serious injury, or anything else that feels urgent — call your
          local emergency number (911 in the United States) or go to the nearest emergency room right
          away. Do not rely on Pre, and do not wait.
        </p>

        <h2>You're taking on the risk</h2>
        <p>
          Physical activity carries inherent risk, including the risk of injury. By using Pre and
          following its guidance, you accept that risk and take full responsibility for your own health
          and safety. To the fullest extent permitted by law, TrainStack is not liable for any injury,
          harm, or loss that results from your use of the app or from following its sessions. Nothing
          here excludes or limits liability that can't be excluded under applicable law. Always use your
          own judgment, work within your limits, and stop when you need to.
        </p>

        <h2>A note on the AI</h2>
        <p>
          Pre's sessions are generated by an AI system from the information you give it. AI can be wrong,
          incomplete, or simply not right for your situation. Treat what Pre produces as a starting point
          for general fitness — not as instructions from a healthcare provider who has assessed you.
        </p>

        <h2>How this fits with our other policies</h2>
        <p>
          This disclaimer is part of, and should be read alongside, our
          <a href="/terms" style="color: var(--color-accent);">Terms of Service</a> and
          <a href="/privacy" style="color: var(--color-accent);">Privacy Policy</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>Questions</h2>
        <p>
          If anything here is unclear, write to us at
          <a href="mailto:support@trypre.app" style="color: var(--color-accent);">support@trypre.app</a>.
          When it comes to your health, though, the right person to ask is a qualified professional.
        </p>

      </div>
    </article>
  </main>
</MarketingLayout>

<style>
  .legal-prose h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    line-height: 1.3;
    margin-top: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .legal-prose h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.3;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .legal-prose p {
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .legal-prose ul {
    list-style: disc;
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .legal-prose li {
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
  }

  .legal-prose a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }
</style>
